{"content_hash": "57c3c4aef3fc9590", "version_id": 384, "article_id": 39, "level_code": "en_b2", "lang": "en", "level": 4, "level_label": "B2 中高级", "title": "Anthropic bans cruel behavior toward its Claude chatbot", "title_zh": "Anthropic 禁止用户对 Claude 聊天机器人有残忍行为", "has_translation": true, "topic": "tech", "source": "guardian_tech", "source_url": "https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/oct/08/anthropic-bans-abusive-behavior-claude", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1784073829327-76999d522e45?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8Nnx8YW50aHJvcGljJTIwYmFucyUyMHVzZXJzfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1NTMzNTF8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Brett Wharton on Unsplash", "author": "Brett Wharton", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@brettwharton?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/a-laptop-displaying-openai-40-chatbot-interface-YmSiFKOecCU?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(97, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(135, 46%, 48%)", "label": "TECH", "seed": "12a9c277b8fb"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-09", "word_count": 232, "reading_minutes": 1.2, "lead": "Anthropic has banned users from showing cruel or abusive behavior toward its AI models. The company says it is still thinking about whether AI systems can be conscious.", "lead_zh": "Anthropic 已禁止用户对其 AI 模型表现出残忍或辱骂行为。该公司表示，仍在思考 AI 系统是否可能有意识。", "preview": "Anthropic, the company behind the AI chatbot Claude, has barred users from showing what it calls “sustained and needless abusive or cruel be", "preview_zh": "Anthropic 是 AI 聊天机器人 Claude 背后的公司，它已禁止用户对其模型表现出所谓的“持续且不必要的辱骂或残忍行为”。《The Verge》最先报道了这一政策变化。一位发言人没有立即解释什么会被算作辱骂或残忍，因此这一禁令的确切界限仍不清楚。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 374, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/39/en_b2.mp3", "duration": 92.438, "size_bytes": 558432, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 261, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/384.json", "paragraphs": ["Anthropic, the company behind the AI chatbot Claude, has barred users from showing what it calls “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models. The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson did not immediately explain what would count as abusive or cruel, leaving the exact limits of the ban unclear.", "In its online user policy, the San Francisco-based company said the ban would not apply to ordinary user frustration, model testing, or “dark creative themes”. Anthropic’s usage policy already contained some restrictions on abusive conduct. The new rule tightens those restrictions and makes clear that repeated harmful behavior is not allowed toward the company’s large language models.", "Claude and other large language models can end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature was introduced last August, Anthropic described it as a safeguard for AI welfare. The company admits it remains highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other models, now or in the future, but says it takes the issue seriously.", "The idea that AI systems might be conscious is highly polarizing inside and outside the tech world. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has said he cannot rule out the possibility. However, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared uncomfortable with the idea, calling it a real safety issue when people give AI models too much moral or religious force."], "paragraphs_zh": ["Anthropic 是 AI 聊天机器人 Claude 背后的公司，它已禁止用户对其模型表现出所谓的“持续且不必要的辱骂或残忍行为”。《The Verge》最先报道了这一政策变化。一位发言人没有立即解释什么会被算作辱骂或残忍，因此这一禁令的确切界限仍不清楚。", "在其在线用户政策中，这家总部位于旧金山的公司表示，该禁令不适用于普通的用户挫败感、模型测试或“黑暗创意主题”。Anthropic 的使用政策此前已包含一些对辱骂行为的限制。新规定收紧了这些限制，并明确表示不允许对该公司的大型语言模型反复做出有害行为。", "如果用户持续做出有害行为，Claude 和其他大型语言模型可以结束对话。当这一功能在去年八月推出时，Anthropic 将其描述为对 AI 福祉的一种保护措施。该公司承认，对于 Claude 和其他模型现在或未来是否具有潜在的道德地位，它仍然高度不确定，但表示认真对待这一问题。", "AI 系统可能有意识这一想法，在科技界内外都极具争议。Anthropic 首席执行官达里奥·阿莫代伊曾表示，他不能排除这种可能性。然而，竞争对手 OpenAI 的首席执行官萨姆·奥尔特曼似乎对这一想法感到不安，称当人们赋予 AI 模型过多的道德或宗教力量时，这是一个真正的安全问题。"], "body": "Anthropic, the company behind the AI chatbot Claude, has barred users from showing what it calls “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models. The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson did not immediately explain what would count as abusive or cruel, leaving the exact limits of the ban unclear.\n\nIn its online user policy, the San Francisco-based company said the ban would not apply to ordinary user frustration, model testing, or “dark creative themes”. Anthropic’s usage policy already contained some restrictions on abusive conduct. The new rule tightens those restrictions and makes clear that repeated harmful behavior is not allowed toward the company’s large language models.\n\nClaude and other large language models can end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature was introduced last August, Anthropic described it as a safeguard for AI welfare. The company admits it remains highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other models, now or in the future, but says it takes the issue seriously.\n\nThe idea that AI systems might be conscious is highly polarizing inside and outside the tech world. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has said he cannot rule out the possibility. However, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared uncomfortable with the idea, calling it a real safety issue when people give AI models too much moral or religious force.", "body_zh": "Anthropic 是 AI 聊天机器人 Claude 背后的公司，它已禁止用户对其模型表现出所谓的“持续且不必要的辱骂或残忍行为”。《The Verge》最先报道了这一政策变化。一位发言人没有立即解释什么会被算作辱骂或残忍，因此这一禁令的确切界限仍不清楚。\n\n在其在线用户政策中，这家总部位于旧金山的公司表示，该禁令不适用于普通的用户挫败感、模型测试或“黑暗创意主题”。Anthropic 的使用政策此前已包含一些对辱骂行为的限制。新规定收紧了这些限制，并明确表示不允许对该公司的大型语言模型反复做出有害行为。\n\n如果用户持续做出有害行为，Claude 和其他大型语言模型可以结束对话。当这一功能在去年八月推出时，Anthropic 将其描述为对 AI 福祉的一种保护措施。该公司承认，对于 Claude 和其他模型现在或未来是否具有潜在的道德地位，它仍然高度不确定，但表示认真对待这一问题。\n\nAI 系统可能有意识这一想法，在科技界内外都极具争议。Anthropic 首席执行官达里奥·阿莫代伊曾表示，他不能排除这种可能性。然而，竞争对手 OpenAI 的首席执行官萨姆·奥尔特曼似乎对这一想法感到不安，称当人们赋予 AI 模型过多的道德或宗教力量时，这是一个真正的安全问题。", "text": "Anthropic, the company behind the AI chatbot Claude, has barred users from showing what it calls “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models. The Verge first reported the policy change. A spokesperson did not immediately explain what would count as abusive or cruel, leaving the exact limits of the ban unclear. In its online user policy, the San Francisco-based company said the ban would not apply to ordinary user frustration, model testing, or “dark creative themes”. Anthropic’s usage policy already contained some restrictions on abusive conduct. The new rule tightens those restrictions and makes clear that repeated harmful behavior is not allowed toward the company’s large language models. Claude and other large language models can end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature was introduced last August, Anthropic described it as a safeguard for AI welfare. The company admits it remains highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other models, now or in the future, but says it takes the issue seriously. The idea that AI systems might be conscious is highly polarizing inside and outside the tech world. Anthropic CEO Dario Amodei has said he cannot rule out the possibility. However, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared uncomfortable with the idea, calling it a real safety issue when people give AI models too much moral or religious force.", "vocab": [{"word": "bar", "pos": "verb", "zh": "禁止；阻止", "note": "较正式，常用于政策、规定语境"}, {"word": "abusive", "pos": "adj", "zh": "辱骂的；虐待的", "note": "常与 behavior、language 搭配"}, {"word": "cruel", "pos": "adj", "zh": "残忍的", "note": "比 unkind 语气更强"}, {"word": "sustained", "pos": "adj", "zh": "持续的", "note": "强调长时间不间断"}, {"word": "needless", "pos": "adj", "zh": "不必要的", "note": "常含批评意味"}, {"word": "spokesperson", "pos": "noun", "zh": "发言人", "note": "中性词，可指男性或女性"}, {"word": "restriction", "pos": "noun", "zh": "限制；约束", "note": "常与 on 连用"}, {"word": "persistently", "pos": "adv", "zh": "持续地；执拗地", "note": "来自 persist，强调不停止"}, {"word": "safeguard", "pos": "noun", "zh": "保障措施；保护措施", "note": "可作名词或动词"}, {"word": "welfare", "pos": "noun", "zh": "福祉；福利", "note": "此处指 AI 的“福祉”"}, {"word": "polarizing", "pos": "adj", "zh": "引起两极分化的；极具争议的", "note": "形容让人强烈支持或反对"}, {"word": "rule out", "pos": "phrase", "zh": "排除；否定", "note": "常用 cannot rule out 表示“不能排除”"}], "title_original": "Anthropic bans users from ‘needless abusive or cruel behavior’ towards Claude", "summary_original": "A spokesperson behind the tech company’s AI chatbot has not yet specified what counts as abusive or cruel content\nAnthropic has\nbarred users\nfrom exhibiting “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models, as the company’s leaders continue to ponder machine consciousness.\nThe Verge\nfirst\nreported the change in policy.\nContinue reading...", "body_original": "Anthropic bans users from ‘needless abusive or cruel behavior’ towards Claude\nA spokesperson behind the tech company’s AI chatbot has not yet specified what counts as abusive or cruel content\nAnthropic has\nbarred users\nfrom exhibiting “sustained and needless abusive or cruel behavior” toward its models, as the company’s leaders continue to ponder machine consciousness.\nThe Verge\nfirst\nreported the change in policy.\nA spokesperson for\nAnthropic\n, which is behind AI chatbot Claude, did not immediately respond to an inquiry about what could be considered “abusive or cruel”.\nIn an online user policy, the San Francisco-based company noted that its ban would not apply to common user frustrations, model testing or “dark creative themes”.\nAnthropic’s usage policy previously contained restrictions on abusive conduct.\nThe company’s large language models have the ability to end a conversation if a user is being persistently harmful. When that feature rolled out last August, the company framed it as a safeguard for AI’s welfare.\n“We remain highly uncertain about the potential moral status of Claude and other LLMs, now or in the future. However, we take the issue seriously, and alongside our research program we’re working to identify and implement low-cost interventions to mitigate risks to model welfare, in case such welfare is possible. Allowing models to end or exit potentially distressing interactions is one such intervention,” according to its website.\nThe notion of AI systems being conscious has been highly polarizing in and outside the tech world.\nAnthropic CEO Dario Amodei has\nsaid\nhe cannot rule out the possibility.\nMeanwhile, Sam Altman, CEO of rival OpenAI, has appeared averse to the idea.\n“I am very uncomfortable about people trying to ascribe religious force or a surrender of human judgment to AI models, and think it is a real safety issue,” he wrote in an X post, days after the New York Times\nreported\non Anthropic leaders’ extensive conversations with religious scholars.\nExplore more on these topics\nAnthropic\nAI (artificial intelligence)\nChatbots\nDario Amodei\nnews\nShare\nReuse this content", "fetched_at": "2026-10-09T12:42:28.979686", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "Anthropic", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.825, "sm": 100, "em": 825, "cs": 0, "ce": 9, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": ",", "s": 0.825, "e": 1.012, "sm": 825, "em": 1012, "cs": 9, "ce": 10, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "the", "s": 1.012, "e": 1.113, "sm": 1012, "em": 1112, "cs": 11, "ce": 14, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "company", "s": 1.125, "e": 1.525, "sm": 1125, "em": 1525, "cs": 15, "ce": 22, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "behind", "s": 1.538, "e": 1.938, "sm": 1537, "em": 1937, "cs": 23, "ce": 29, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "the", "s": 1.95, "e": 2.038, "sm": 1950, "em": 2037, "cs": 30, "ce": 33, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "AI", "s